@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`

-- Chuong VII (Dieu 155-157): amendment of the Investment Law, commencement, transition. These are the
-- provisions on which the vintages turn: Law 139/2025/QH15 replaces Dieu 156(2), amends Dieu 156(3), adds
-- Dieu 156(4), replaces Dieu 157(2) and (from V3) repeals Dieu 155. Every rule here takes TWO dates: the
-- rule-version axis (which text governs, RULES EFFECTIVE DATE, pinned in a test by EVAL UNDER RULES
-- EFFECTIVE AT) and, where the question is "was it in force on day D", the day D as an explicit input.
-- (A question about D in 2029 under the V1 text is the question what the Law as made said about 2029.)

§ `Chuong VII: Dieu khoan thi hanh`

§§ `Dieu 155: amendment of Appendix IV of the Investment Law`

-- Dieu 155 adds two lines to the Investment Law's list of conditional business lines. Law 139/2025/QH15
-- Dieu 2(8) repeals Dieu 155 from 1 July 2026 (V3). The repeal does not say whether the lines the Appendix
-- now carries stay there, and the Investment Law is not among the sources: V3 answers with silence.
@@qb 516 522
@@qa 339 339
@ref Dieu 155 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:516-522; src:law139-2025-qh15:339)
GIVEN l IS A `A business line of the Investment Law Appendix IV`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 155: the Law lists the business line as a conditional investment business line` l MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V3`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 155 is repealed by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(8) from 1 July 2026; the Law does not say whether the lines it added to the Investment Law Appendix IV remain"
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN CONSIDER l
                WHEN `insurance brokerage`             THEN TRUE
                WHEN `ancillary insurance services`    THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

§§ `Dieu 156: commencement`

@@qb 524 525
@ref Dieu 156 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:524-525)
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 156(1): the date the Law takes effect` MEANS `the date Law 08/2022/QH15 took effect (V1 begins)`

-- Dieu 156(2). V1: Dieu 86(3), 94(4)-(5), 95, 99(3)-(4) and Dieu 109-114, 116 all take effect on 1 January
-- 2028. V2 (Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(14)(a)): the first group on 1 January 2028, the second group (109-114,
-- 116) on 1 January 2031.
@@qb 528 530
@@qa 291 295
@ref Dieu 156 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:528-530; src:law139-2025-qh15:291-295)
GIVEN p IS A `A provision with a deferred commencement`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 156(2): the date the provision takes effect` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN CONSIDER p
                WHEN `Dieu 109` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 110` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 111` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 112` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 113` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 114` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                WHEN `Dieu 116` THEN YMD 2031 1 1
                OTHERWISE YMD 2028 1 1
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN YMD 2028 1 1
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

GIVEN p IS A `A provision with a deferred commencement`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` p `the day in question` MEANS
    `the day in question` AT LEAST `Dieu 156(2): the date the provision takes effect` p

-- Dieu 156(3). The old Law 24/2000/QH10 ends on the commencement, except Dieu 157(1) of this Law and the
-- old provisions listed. V1: old Dieu 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 83, 94 and 98, all to the end of 2027. V2 (Law
-- 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(14)(b)): old Dieu 94 to the end of 2027; old Dieu 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 83 and 98 to the
-- end of 2030. Before the commencement the old Law governs everything.
@@qb 531 537
@@qa 297 304
@ref Dieu 156 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:531-537; src:law139-2025-qh15:297-304)
GIVEN q IS A `A provision of the old Law 24/2000/QH10`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 156(3): the old Law provision is in force on the day` q `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` BELOW `the date Law 08/2022/QH15 took effect (V1 begins)`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
                THEN CONSIDER q
                     WHEN `old Dieu 94` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 77` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 78` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 79` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 80` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 81` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 83` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 98` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
                     OTHERWISE FALSE
                IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
                THEN CONSIDER q
                     WHEN `old Dieu 77` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 78` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 79` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 80` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 81` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 83` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 94` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     WHEN `old Dieu 98` THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31
                     OTHERWISE FALSE
                OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Dieu 156(4), added by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(14)(c): from 1 January 2028 to the end of 31 December 2030
-- insurers track capital, compute the capital adequacy ratio and plan capital increases as the Minister
-- of Finance prescribes. V1 has no such paragraph.
@@qa 305 310
@ref Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1 (src:law139-2025-qh15:305-310)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 156(4): the interim capital duty applies on the day` `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
    THEN `the day in question` AT LEAST YMD 2028 1 1 AND `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 156(4) does not exist in V1: it was added by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(14)(c) from 1 January 2026"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 156(4): the Minister of Finance's rules on tracking capital, the capital adequacy ratio and the plan to raise capital` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 156(4) leaves the content of the interim capital duty to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 157: transitional provisions`

-- Dieu 157(1). A contract made before the commencement and still running goes on under the law in force
-- when it was made, unless the parties agree to amend it to conform to this Law and to apply this Law.
@@qb 539 543
@ref Dieu 157 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:539-543)
GIVEN c IS A `A contract made before the commencement`
GIVETH A `A governing text`
`Dieu 157(1): the text that governs the contract` c MEANS
    IF c's `date the contract was made` ABOVE YMD 2022 12 31
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 157(1) concerns a contract made before the commencement on 1 January 2023"
    ELSE IF NOT c's `the contract is still running on 1 January 2023`
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 157(1) concerns a contract that still has a term to run at the commencement"
         ELSE IF c's `the parties agreed to amend it to conform to this Law and to apply this Law`
              THEN `Law 08/2022/QH15`
              ELSE `the law in force when the contract was made`

-- Dieu 157(2). An agent certificate issued before the commencement may be used until the end of 31 December
-- 2025 (V1) and, by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(15), until the end of 30 June 2026 (V2, V3).
-- Dieu 157(3): the other certificates "duoc tiep tuc su dung" (may continue to be used) with no end date.
@@qb 544 549
@@qa 312 317
@ref Dieu 157 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:544-549; src:law139-2025-qh15:312-317)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of certificate issued before the commencement`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 157(2)-(3): the certificate issued before the commencement may still be used on the day` k `the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN CONSIDER k
                WHEN `an insurance agent certificate`
                     THEN IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
                          THEN `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2026 6 30
                          ELSE `the day in question` AT MOST YMD 2025 12 31
                OTHERWISE TRUE
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 157(2): the Minister of Finance's rules on converting agent certificates issued before the commencement` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 157(2) delegates the conversion of agent certificates to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

-- Dieu 157(4). From 1 January 2023 insurers stop contributing to the Insured Protection Fund.
@@qb 550 552
@ref Dieu 157 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:550-552)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 157(4): the insurer must contribute to the Insured Protection Fund on the day` `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the date Law 08/2022/QH15 took effect (V1 begins)`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 157(4) says only that contributions stop from 1 January 2023; the contribution before it is the old Law's, not among the sources"

-- Dieu 157(5). The whole balance of the Insured Protection Fund is managed by the Ministry of Finance to
-- protect insured persons if an insurer is insolvent or bankrupt; the Government details its management and use.
@@qb 553 562
@ref Dieu 157 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:553-562)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 157(5): the Government's rules on managing and using the balance of the Insured Protection Fund` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 157(5)(b) delegates the management and use of the balance to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"
